    "mutations": [
      {
        "body": "The Grotesque Tree should read as an immediate, dangerous landmark in the garden: its bark is armor-tough, its branches are thick with thorns, and it attacks any creature that comes within 30 feet. It also retaliates against ranged attacks, tends to focus the nearest enemy, and stops being hostile once it is no longer under imminent threat.\n\nIf you want to seed a clue without giving it away to the players, keep the precious metal leaves strictly behind a Perception gate. The tree can hint at something valuable glittering on odd branches, but do not put the metal leaves in read-aloud; save them for the successful check or for post-fight searching.",
        "documentId": "doc:small-slice-dogfood",
        "expectedContentSha256": null,
        "kind": "gm-note",
        "locator": {
          "afterHeading": "Area 5: Arrive Hempholm"
        },
        "op": "insert_callout",
        "previewMarkdown": "> [!GM-NOTE]\n> The Grotesque Tree should read as an immediate, dangerous landmark in the garden: its bark is armor-tough, its branches are thick with thorns, and it attacks any creature that comes within 30 feet. It also retaliates against ranged attacks, tends to focus the nearest enemy, and stops being hostile once it is no longer under imminent threat.\n>\n> If you want to seed a clue without giving it away to the players, keep the precious metal leaves strictly behind a Perception gate. The tree can hint at something valuable glittering on odd branches, but do not put the metal leaves in read-aloud; save them for the successful check or for post-fight searching.",
